    "windows-gfx1151": {
      "blocked": true,
      "blocked_reason": "MPI runtime absent and not installable without a person. ESPResSo hard-requires MPI 3.0; on Windows that means MS-MPI. Verified absent on this host 2026-08-20: no 'C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft MPI' directory, no mpiexec on PATH, no C:\\Windows\\System32\\msmpi.dll. The MS-MPI redistributable installs only via msmpisetup.exe, which requires administrator elevation that automated validation does not have, and there is no user-mode/portable MS-MPI. Scope note, stated plainly: NO build was attempted on this host -- the MPI prerequisite was checked first and is absent, so a build could not have linked. This matches the already-recorded determination on windows-gfx1101 and windows-gfx1201 (a different physical machine), so the obstacle is the Windows platform's MPI packaging rather than anything about this GPU or the port. UNBLOCKING IS CHEAP AND IS A PERSON'S CALL: installing MS-MPI on this host with admin rights would very likely make espresso validatable here, which is a better outcome than a waiver. See the suggested waiver for the alternative.",
      "validated_sha": null,
